# 3. AUTHENTICATION & FIRST ADMIN SYSTEM

Build a secure registration and login system.

### First Registration Rule

The first successfully registered account must automatically become the Main Admin / Super Admin.

This must be implemented through secure server-side database logic.

Never rely on frontend registration order, browser storage, or user-submitted role values.

### Registration Fields

- Full Name.
- Email Address.
- Phone Number.
- Password.
- Confirm Password.
- Optional Profile Picture.

### Registration Logic

1. First registered user becomes Main Admin.
2. Every subsequent user becomes Pending User.
3. Pending users cannot access private business information.
4. Main Admin receives new registration notifications.
5. Main Admin can approve or reject users.
6. Approved users can access permitted modules.
7. Rejected users cannot access the application.
8. Suspended users immediately lose access.

### Authentication Features

- Email and password login.
- Secure password reset.
- Email verification.
- Secure logout.
- Session management.
- Optional account recovery.
- Biometric / Passkey login.

Implement secure role-based access control at the backend and database level.

